203.m:
Homage to you who hold the mace in hand, O Viṣṇu; homage to you who hold the conch in hand!
I see this form of yours adorned with tangible emblems;
I do not know that supreme [form] of yours; be gracious, O Supreme Lord!

206.m:
Vyāsa said:
Then, having bowed, delighted, he returned from home to Śambhu;
then, seeing his banner broken, rejoiced, he experienced supreme joy.

The Blessed Lord said:
May this Bāṇa, to whom a boon was given by you, live, O Śaṅkara;
out of respect for your words, this disc has been turned back by me.
